From a081e78a79d410b63da0e919331e15889c1ce26f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:50:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Wire multi-service transactions into
 edit/detail/receipt/reports and fix RPC grant + trigger bugs

Completes the "Add New Service" feature across the rest of the app: editing
an order can now add/remove additional service lines (via
replace_transaction_service_items), the transaction detail page and printed
receipts show each additional line with its own add-ons, and kg/report
totals (Home "kg" stat, ReportsManager) include additional-service weight
alongside the primary service.

Also fixes two real bugs surfaced by the new pglite backend tests, both of
which would have blocked the feature in production, not just in tests:

- private.replace_transaction_service_items_rows was revoked from
  authenticated with no grant back. Since both public wrapper RPCs that
  call it are security invoker, the invoking role needs its own EXECUTE
  grant on this private helper regardless of it being security definer -
  security definer only affects privileges inside the function body, not
  whether the caller may invoke it. Added the missing grant (safe: the
  private schema isn't exposed via PostgREST, so this only enables calls
  from other server-side SQL, matching the existing
  private.has_staff_permission / private.can_view_transaction pattern).

- private.consume_transaction_service_items_inventory() was missing the
  "only run on transition to completed" guard that the equivalent
  primary-service trigger has, so it fired (and could reject the order for
  insufficient stock) on every order_status change instead of only at
  completion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
